{
  "$comment": [
    "Brands that phishing actually imitates. Used by the `typosquat` and `deceptive-subdomain`",
    "checks (PLAN.md §2).",
    "",
    "`domain` is the registrable domain we compare against. `label` is the part before the TLD —",
    "that is what edit distance runs on, because 'paypa1.com' and 'paypa1.net' are the same trick.",
    "",
    "Keep this list SHORT and high-value. Every entry is a false-positive surface: a legitimate",
    "site whose name is one edit away from a brand here gets flagged. Only add a brand that is",
    "both widely imitated and distinctive enough that near-misses are genuinely suspicious.",
    "Short labels (<5 chars) are excluded from edit-distance matching in the check itself.",
    "",
    "`regional: true` — the brand genuinely runs country sites (amazon.de, paypal.co.uk), so its",
    "label on a two-letter ccTLD is not by itself impersonation. Without the flag, `roblox.com.do`",
    "and `roblox.ly` are exactly what they look like: someone else's domain wearing the name.",
    "`homoglyphOnly` — only lookalike characters count, not plain edits: one edit from 'icloud'",
    "is every '?cloud' company (pcloud, qcloud, ucloud), while 'icl0ud' is still caught.",
    "`notTypos` — registrable labels that are one edit from the brand but are ordinary words or",
    "real, unrelated companies ('cloud' is not a typo of 'icloud')."
  ],
  "brands": [
    { "label": "paypal", "domain": "paypal.com", "regional": true },
